Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Homepage: http://www.pnetlab.com/
Description: PNetLab patched bridge module (group-MAC forwarding)
 Rebuilds the kernel bridge module via DKMS with BR_GROUPFWD_RESTRICTED
 cleared, so a bridge's group_fwd_mask can forward all 01:80:c2:00:00:0X
 reserved group MACs (STP, MAC pause, LACP/slow protocols). This lets
 emulated switches connected through the host Linux bridges that PNetLab
 builds per lab network form LACP EtherChannels and exchange pause frames —
 impossible with the stock module, which hard-restricts those bits.
 .
 The module installs under updates/ (outranking the in-tree bridge.ko) and
 is rebuilt automatically on every kernel upgrade. The engine writes
 group_fwd_mask 65535 with a 65528 fallback, so labs work with or without it.

